            <ArticleTitle>Intra peritoneal rectal tear: delayed presentation in a battered baby.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a two and a half year old child who presented with an acute abdomen two days after a spoon was forcefully inserted per rectum. The child recovered after repair of the rectal tear and a temporary sigmoid colostomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
